{
  "title": "erasure across stores",
  "question": "What each erase entry point (graph, prefix, ID list, relationship list, all, and the delete_edge bypass) removes, keeps and returns in every store the ontology names, which names it refuses before any change, and how its own transaction, the store's 500-entry chunks, the post-commit route drop and the caller's transaction change the outcome",
